  Name: "Aluminum 6061-T6"
  Description: >-
    Precipitation-hardened wrought aluminum-magnesium-silicon alloy (Al-Mg-Si),
    one of the most common general-purpose structural aluminum alloys.
    Physical and mechanical properties: Wikipedia article "6061 aluminium alloy"
    (CC-BY-SA-4.0), accessed 2026-05.
    Machinability data derived from FreeCAD core 'AluminumWroughtAlloy.FCMat'
    (Jonas Bähr, CC-BY-3.0, sourced from Tabellenbuch Zerspantechnik
    ISBN 978-3-7585-1315-2). The 50% "favorable condition" multiplier on the
    carbide surface speed in the source has been removed to give a more
    conservative uncoated-carbide roughing default; original 180 m/min base
    value is used instead of the bumped 270 m/min.
    Values are typical room-temperature properties. Specific lot/temper data
    may deviate; consult vendor mill certificates for safety-critical use.
  SourceURL: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/6061_aluminium_alloy"
